From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: configure output parameters on first CAPTURE streamon after an early flush

The gen1 seek_resume path skips session_set_config_params() on CAPTURE streamon
under the assumption that output port parameters were already configured on an
earlier CAPTURE streamon. However, if a client flushes the decoder after OUTPUT
streamon but before the first CAPTURE streamon (while IRIS_INST_SUB_FIRST_IPSC
is still set), skipping output configuration causes the firmware to fail with
HFI_ERR_SESSION_INSUFFICIENT_RESOURCES (0x1009).

Always configure output port parameters on CAPTURE streamon when
IRIS_INST_SUB_FIRST_IPSC is set.

Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [firmware workaround]
---
diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
index 15e2164d3..b638d58c3 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_vdec.c
@@ -432,8 +432,12 @@ int iris_vdec_streamon_output(struct iris_inst *inst)
 	const struct iris_hfi_session_ops *hfi_ops = inst->hfi_session_ops;
 	int ret;
 
-	/* seek_mode=1: the output port is configured and running, only the DPBs go back */
-	if (!inst->seek_resume) {
+	/*
+	 * seek_mode=1: the output port is configured and running, only the DPBs go back.
+	 * Not after a source change: a flush before the first CAPTURE streamon leaves
+	 * seek_resume set with an output port that was never configured.
+	 */
+	if (!inst->seek_resume || inst->sub_state & IRIS_INST_SUB_FIRST_IPSC) {
 		ret = hfi_ops->session_set_config_params(inst, V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE_MPLANE);
 		if (ret)
 			return ret;
